{"id":"mahabharata-2-050","work":"mahabharata","part":2,"partName":"सभापर्व","partNameEn":"Sabha Parva","unit":50,"title":"पञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 50 · Dhritarashtra counsels; Duryodhana insists","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra urges his son not to hate the Pandavas, who share his ancestry and do him no wrong. Duryodhana replies that for a kshatriya victory is dharma, that a rival's growth is a disease, and that he cannot bear to live while the Pandavas prosper.","kn":"ವಂಶವನ್ನು ಹಂಚಿಕೊಂಡ, ತನಗೆ ಯಾವ ಅಪಕಾರವೂ ಮಾಡದ ಪಾಂಡವರನ್ನು ದ್ವೇಷಿಸಬೇಡ ಎಂದು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನು ಮಗನನ್ನು ಬೇಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕ್ಷತ್ರಿಯನಿಗೆ ಜಯವೇ ಧರ್ಮ, ಶತ್ರುವಿನ ಏಳಿಗೆ ರೋಗ, ಪಾಂಡವರು ಏಳಿಗೆ ಹೊಂದುತ್ತಿರುವಾಗ ತಾನು ಬದುಕಲಾರೆ ಎಂದು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನು ಉತ್ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र पुत्र से आग्रह करते हैं कि पाण्डवों से द्वेष न करे, जो उसी वंश के हैं और उसका कोई अहित नहीं करते। दुर्योधन उत्तर देता है कि क्षत्रिय के लिए विजय ही धर्म है, शत्रु की वृद्धि रोग है, और पाण्डवों के फलते-फूलते वह जीवित नहीं रह सकता।","te":"వంశాన్ని పంచుకున్న, తనకు ఏ అపకారం చేయని పాండవులను ద్వేషించవద్దని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు కుమారుని కోరతాడు. క్షత్రియునికి జయమే ధర్మం, శత్రువు వృద్ధి రోగం, పాండవులు వర్ధిల్లుతుండగా తాను బతకలేనని దుర్యోధనుడు బదులిస్తాడు.","ta":"குலத்தைப் பகிர்ந்த, தனக்கு எந்தத் தீங்கும் செய்யாத பாண்டவர்களை வெறுக்க வேண்டாம் என்று திருதராஷ்டிரன் மகனை வேண்டுகிறான். க்ஷத்ரியனுக்கு வெற்றியே தர்மம், பகைவனின் வளர்ச்சி ஒரு நோய், பாண்டவர்கள் செழிக்கும்போது தன்னால் வாழ முடியாது என்று துரியோதனன் பதில் சொல்கிறான்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവർ തന്റെ വംശജരും തനിക്ക് ഒരു ദോഷവും ചെയ്യാത്തവരുമാണെന്ന് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ മകനെ ഉപദേശിക്കുന്നു. ക്ഷത്രിയന് വിജയമാണ് ധർമ്മമെന്നും, ശത്രുവിന്റെ വളർച്ച ഒരു രോഗമാണെന്നും, പാണ്ഡവർ ഐശ്വര്യത്തോടെ കഴിയുമ്പോൾ ജീവിക്കാൻ തനിക്ക് കഴിയില്ലെന്നും ദുര്യോധനൻ മറുപടി നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 2.50; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Apr 19 2006","sections":[{"title":"द्यूतपर्व","titleEn":"Dyuta Parva (The dice game)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"त्वं वै ज्येष्ठो ज्यैष्ठिनेयः पुत्र मा पाण्डवान्द्विषः ।\nद्वेष्टा ह्यसुखमादत्ते यथैव निधनं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are the eldest, my son, born of the eldest wife. Do not hate the Pandavas; a hater takes on misery, and it is as good as his own death."}},{"n":2,"text":"अव्युत्पन्नं समानार्थं तुल्यमित्रं युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nअद्विषन्तं कथं द्विष्यात्त्वादृशो भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira is guileless, shares your aims, is a friend like any other, and hates no one. How could a man like you, best of Bharatas, hate him?"}},{"n":3,"text":"तुल्याभिजनवीर्यश्च कथं भ्रातुः श्रियं नृप ।\nपुत्र कामयसे मोहान्मैवं भूः शाम्य साध्विह ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are equal to him in birth and valor, so why, my son, do you covet your brother's prosperity out of delusion? Do not be so; calm down and act rightly."}},{"n":4,"text":"अथ यज्ञविभूतिं तां काङ्क्षसे भरतर्षभ ।\nऋत्विजस्तव तन्वन्तु सप्ततन्तुं महाध्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you long for the splendor of that sacrifice, best of Bharatas, let your own priests perform the great seven-fold rite for you."}},{"n":5,"text":"आहरिष्यन्ति राजानस्तवापि विपुलं धनम् ।\nप्रीत्या च बहुमानाच्च रत्नान्याभरणानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings will bring you too immense wealth, jewels and ornaments, out of affection and respect."}},{"n":6,"text":"अनर्थाचरितं तात परस्वस्पृहणं भृशम् ।\nस्वसंतुष्टः स्वधर्मस्थो यः स वै सुखमेधते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Greedy desire for another's property is wrongful conduct, my son. He who is content with his own and stays in his duty prospers happily."}},{"n":7,"text":"अव्यापारः परार्थेषु नित्योद्योगः स्वकर्मसु ।\nउद्यमो रक्षणे स्वेषामेतद्वैभवलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not meddling in others' affairs, constant effort in one's own work, and diligence in protecting one's own people: these are the marks of prosperity."}},{"n":8,"text":"विपत्तिष्वव्यथो दक्षो नित्यमुत्थानवान्नरः ।\nअप्रमत्तो विनीतात्मा नित्यं भद्राणि पश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who is unshaken in misfortune, skilled, always energetic, careful and disciplined always sees good things."}},{"n":9,"text":"अन्तर्वेद्यां ददद्वित्तं कामाननुभवन्प्रियान् ।\nक्रीडन्स्त्रीभिर्निरातङ्कः प्रशाम्य भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give wealth at the sacrificial altar, enjoy the pleasures you love, and sport fearlessly with women. Be at peace, best of Bharatas."}},{"text":"दुर्योधन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"जानन्वै मोहयसि मां नावि नौरिव संयता ।\nस्वार्थे किं नावधानं ते उताहो द्वेष्टि मां भवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing all this, you still bewilder me, like a tied-up boat leading another boat. Do you not care about your own good, or do you hate me?"}},{"n":11,"text":"न सन्तीमे धार्तराष्ट्रा येषां त्वमनुशासिता ।\nभविष्यमर्थमाख्यासि सदा त्वं कृत्यमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is as if these Dhartarashtras, whom you are meant to guide, did not exist; you always speak of some future good for yourself."}},{"n":12,"text":"परप्रणेयोऽग्रणीर्हि यश्च मार्गात्प्रमुह्यति ।\nपन्थानमनुगच्छेयुः कथं तस्य पदानुगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A leader who is led by others and loses the road: how could his followers keep to the path?"}},{"n":13,"text":"राजन्परिगतप्रज्ञो वृद्धसेवी जितेन्द्रियः ।\nप्रतिपन्नान्स्वकार्येषु संमोहयसि नो भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, your wisdom is complete and you serve elders and master your senses, yet you thoroughly confuse us who depend on you in our tasks."}},{"n":14,"text":"लोकवृत्ताद्राजवृत्तमन्यदाह बृहस्पतिः ।\nतस्माद्राज्ञा प्रयत्नेन स्वार्थश्चिन्त्यः सदैव हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brihaspati says a king's conduct differs from ordinary conduct. So a king must always diligently think of his own interest."}},{"n":15,"text":"क्षत्रियस्य महाराज जये वृत्तिः समाहिता ।\nस वै धर्मोऽस्त्वधर्मो वा स्ववृत्तौ भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a kshatriya, great king, livelihood rests on victory. Whether it is righteous or not, that is his own way of living, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":16,"text":"प्रकालयेद्दिशः सर्वाः प्रतोदेनेव सारथिः ।\nप्रत्यमित्रश्रियं दीप्तां बुभूषुर्भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who wishes to grow must drive all quarters before him, as a charioteer drives with his goad, and seize the blazing fortune of his enemy."}},{"n":17,"text":"प्रच्छन्नो वा प्रकाशो वा यो योगो रिपुबाधनः ।\nतद्वै शस्त्रं शस्त्रविदां न शस्त्रं छेदनं स्मृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Any means that harms a foe, hidden or open, is the real weapon for those who know weapons; a weapon is not merely what cuts."}},{"n":18,"text":"असंतोषः श्रियो मूलं तस्मात्तं कामयाम्यहम् ।\nसमुच्छ्रये यो यतते स राजन्परमो नयी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Discontent is the root of prosperity, so I desire it. A king who strives to rise is the best statesman."}},{"n":19,"text":"ममत्वं हि न कर्तव्यमैश्वर्ये वा धनेऽपि वा ।\nपूर्वावाप्तं हरन्त्यन्ये राजधर्मं हि तं विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should not feel possessive about rule or wealth, since others take what was won before. Kings know that as the royal duty."}},{"n":20,"text":"अद्रोहे समयं कृत्वा चिच्छेद नमुचेः शिरः ।\nशक्रः सा हि मता तस्य रिपौ वृत्तिः सनातनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Indra made a pact of non-injury and then cut off Namuchi's head. That is the ancient way of dealing with an enemy."}},{"n":21,"text":"द्वावेतौ ग्रसते भूमिः सर्पो बिलशयानिव ।\nराजानं चाविरोद्धारं ब्राह्मणं चाप्रवासिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth swallows two kinds: the king who does not fight, and the brahmin who does not travel, as a snake swallows creatures in its hole."}},{"n":22,"text":"नास्ति वै जातितः शत्रुः पुरुषस्य विशां पते ।\nयेन साधारणी वृत्तिः स शत्रुर्नेतरो जनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"No one is a man's enemy by birth, lord of the people. Whoever shares one's own livelihood is the enemy, no one else."}},{"n":23,"text":"शत्रुपक्षं समृध्यन्तं यो मोहात्समुपेक्षते ।\nव्याधिराप्यायित इव तस्य मूलं छिनत्ति सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who through folly ignores a rising enemy party is like one who feeds a disease, and it cuts him at the root."}},{"n":24,"text":"अल्पोऽपि ह्यरिरत्यन्तं वर्धमानपराक्रमः ।\nवल्मीको मूलज इव ग्रसते वृक्षमन्तिकात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even a small foe whose might keeps growing swallows the tree from near it, like an anthill that grows from its roots."}},{"n":25,"text":"आजमीढ रिपोर्लक्ष्मीर्मा ते रोचिष्ट भारत ।\nएष भारः सत्त्ववतां नयः शिरसि धिष्ठितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Descendant of Ajamidha, do not take pleasure in the enemy's prosperity. This policy of the strong is a burden set on the head."}},{"n":26,"text":"जन्मवृद्धिमिवार्थानां यो वृद्धिमभिकाङ्क्षते ।\nएधते ज्ञातिषु स वै सद्योवृद्धिर्हि विक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who wants to grow as wealth grows from its birth rises among his kin, for valor brings swift gain."}},{"n":27,"text":"नाप्राप्य पाण्डवैश्वर्यं संशयो मे भविष्यति ।\nअवाप्स्ये वा श्रियं तां हि शेष्ये वा निहतो युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Until I gain the Pandavas' sovereignty I will have no peace; either I will win that fortune or lie slain in battle."}},{"n":28,"text":"अतादृशस्य किं मेऽद्य जीवितेन विशां पते ।\nवर्धन्ते पाण्डवा नित्यं वयं तु स्थिरवृद्धयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What use is life to me now, lord, when I am not like them? The Pandavas grow constantly while we hold steady."}}]}]}